[00:00.00] Did you begin to sing about this time? How did that happen?
[00:07.00] Well, when I come back from this trip to the Gulf of Mexico that I told you about,
[00:15.00] then I went back up into the panhandle of Texas, the big wheat belt,
[00:20.00] up around Amarillo, Texas, north of Amarillo, Texas,
[00:23.00] and around Borger and Canadian, Pampa and all those oil fields up in there,
[00:30.00] big oil fields that just broke out and there's a big boom on,
[00:33.00] and a lot of people from down in my country was going out there to get a job of work.
[00:39.00] And times had got pretty hard in Oklahoma and everybody was drifting out that way,
[00:43.00] so I drifted out there with them.
[00:45.00] And when I got out into that country, I got a job about the third day I was there.
[00:52.00] I got a job with a fella that owned a root beer stand, supposedly,
[00:58.00] and he said he'd give me $3 a day to stand behind the counter and sell people root beers.
[01:02.00] So I told him I had intelligence enough to do that, so I got around behind the counter.
[01:09.00] And he told me, he said now in addition to this root beer,
[01:15.00] he said, here's some bottles here of another description.
[01:20.00] And he says if anybody comes up and lays a dollar and a half on the counter here,
[01:27.00] why you reach down and gently and firmly let them have one of these beer bottles.
[01:35.00] One day, McCuriosity got the best of me and I just got the wondering
[01:38.00] what in the devil is in them bottles.
[01:40.00] So I opened up one and tasted of it and it was nothing in the world,
[01:45.00] just purity old and unadulterated corn whiskey.
[01:52.00] So we was wheeling and dealing there in the whiskey business for a long time.
[01:58.00] This guy had a guitar that laid around there
[02:03.00] and a lot of times there wouldn't be any customers in the place.
[02:06.00] I'd grab up this guitar and got the packing around on it.
[02:08.00] I thought it sounded awful pretty.
[02:12.00] And I learned a little old chord.
[02:14.00] I just had a barely chord long and finally learned a few little old songs
[02:19.00] and then I don't know, I just kind of drifted into it.
[02:22.00] I never did own a guitar though.
[02:24.00] What were some of the first songs you began to sing out there in Panhandle?
[02:29.00] Here's an old song here that they sang back down in that country almost everybody knows it.
